EctoPad iOS control correction, 2026-08-13

The first physical build incorrectly treated the yellow C-stick as a
free-look stick. Worse, the iOS LookHold shortcut read Prime's logical look
commands, which are sourced from the left Control Stick while R is held. That
made ordinary left-stick input enter look mode and removed normal movement.

Restore original Metroid Prime/GameCube semantics:

- remove the iOS-only `TouchCStickActsAsLookHold` override from
  `Runtime/World/CPlayer.cpp`;
- leave the left Control Stick on movement;
- leave the yellow C-stick on beam selection through the existing GameCube
  substick path;
- present R as a normal press-and-hold touch button, setting digital R and
  full trigger pressure for the duration of the touch;
- let L or R latch after a half-second continuous touch. A latched shoulder
  turns blue, emits one haptic, stays asserted after release, and unlatches on
  the next tap. Short touches retain normal hold behavior;
- remove the Sunshine-specific "Modern C-stick" toggle from EctoPad's touch
  settings because it is not a Prime control feature.

This does not change controller plumbing or invent a mobile camera model.
Original Prime look/aim remains Control Stick while R is held; L remains
lock-on/strafe.
